// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 8 (Impl-L): GC scoping — the GC→GC
// discharge. A ref to a GC-managed binding ('p', the `new` constructor
// path) stored into a GC-managed destination ('cells', a list literal —
// sn_list_new → gc_track): the normal case. Both sides live in the GC
// heap's memory category (W2A §1.4) — the collector owns the whole
// reference chain, so E-GC-IN-LANE must NOT fire, and the program runs:
// the pushed ref makes the list's length 1.
//
// The lane stays untouched (lane 2 never opened), which the second
// print proves.

blueprint Point {
    int x
    int y
}

fn main() {
    new Point p(x: 1, y: 2)
    list<ptr> cells = []
    cells.push(address(p))
    print(cells.length())
    print(lane_used(2) > 0)
}
